{number: 67}
{title: Pass Me Not, O Gentle Savior}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Pass me not, O gentle Saviour,
Hear my humble cry;
While on the others Thou art calling,
Do not pass me by.
Saviour, saviour,
Hear my humble cry;
While on others Thou art calling,
Do not pass me by.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Let me at Thy throne of mercy
Find a sweet relief;
Kneeling there in deep contrition,
Help my unbelief.
Saviour, saviour,
Hear my humble cry;
While on others Thou art calling,
Do not pass me by.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Trusting only in Thy merit,
Would I seek Thy face,
Heal my wounded, broken spirit,
Save me by Thy grace.
Saviour, saviour,
Hear my humble cry;
While on others Thou art calling,
Do not pass me by.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Thou the spring of all my comfort,
More than life to me,
Whom have I on earth beside Thee?
Whom in heav’n but Thee
Saviour, saviour,
Hear my humble cry;
While on others Thou art calling,
Do not pass me by.
{end_of_verse}
